<p>The United States plans to deploy an American anti-drone system that performed well against Russian drones in Ukraine to the Middle East, aiming to strengthen U.S. defenses against Iranian drones, according to two U.S. officials. Reporting identifies the system as Merops, a compact counter-drone capability the U.S. is moving from the Ukraine battlefield to a region where officials and analysts see a growing threat to people, facilities, and infrastructure.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>System profile: Merops is described as small enough to fit in the back of a midsize pickup truck, making it easier to deploy to dispersed sites.</li><li>How it intercepts: The system “flies drones against drones,” sending an interceptor drone after hostile drones instead of relying only on missiles or guns.</li><li>Targeting step: Merops can identify drones and then close in on them, reflecting a pursuit-style intercept approach.</li><li>Layered defenses: NDTV ties the move to broader U.S. regional defenses, including systems such as Patriot and THAAD as part of layered protection.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. officials (as cited by AP): Two U.S. officials said the U.S. will send the anti-drone system to bolster defenses in the Middle East after it proved effective in Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-will-send-anti-drone-system-to-mideast-after-successful-use-in-ukraine-officials-say'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Firstpost on Merops: Firstpost describes Merops as a mobile, AI-assisted “drone-on-drone” tool designed to keep working even under heavy jamming, a common battlefield constraint. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-plans-to-send-ukraine-proven-anti-drone-system-to-west-asia-13987074.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>The Economist analysis: The Economist argues Ukraine’s experience countering mass Shahed-style attacks could help inform Gulf defenses, and underscores the scale of the drone threat in the region. (<a href='https://www.economist.com/international/2026/03/06/can-ukraine-help-defeat-irans-drone-swarms'>The Economist</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-to-deploy-anti-drone-system-from-ukraine-to-middle-east-to-counter-iran-middle-east-conflict-patriot-and-thaad-missile-systems-shahed-drones-11180437#publisher=newsstand'>US To Deploy Anti Drone System From Ukraine To Middle East To Counter Iran</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-plans-to-send-ukraine-proven-anti-drone-system-to-west-asia-13987074.html'>US plans to send Ukraine-proven anti-drone system to West Asia</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.economist.com/international/2026/03/06/can-ukraine-help-defeat-irans-drone-swarms'>Can Ukraine help defeat Iran’s drone swarms?</a> - economist.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-will-send-anti-drone-system-to-mideast-after-successful-use-in-ukraine-officials-say'>U.S. will send anti-drone system to Mideast after successful use in Ukraine, officials say</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>